<topic id="borders">
  <title>Borders</title>
  <shortdesc>Use border utilities to quickly style the border and border-radius of an element.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Borders</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Color</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Background</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <xmlatt>frame</xmlatt>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">

    <section id="borders">
      <title>Borders</title>
      <p>Use border utilities to add or remove an element’s borders. Choose from all borders or one at a time.</p>
    </section>
    <fig>
      <title>Borders</title>
      <image href="src/borders/borders.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <codeblock>&lt;ph outputclass="border"&gt;...&lt;/ph&gt;
&lt;ph outputclass="border-top"&gt;...&lt;/ph&gt;
&lt;ph outputclass="border-end"&gt;...&lt;/ph&gt;
&lt;ph outputclass="border-bottom"&gt;...&lt;/ph&gt;
&lt;ph outputclass="border-start"&gt;...&lt;/ph&gt;</codeblock>

    <section>
      <title>Border Specialization</title>
      <p>The <xmlatt>border</xmlatt> and <xmlatt
        >rounded</xmlatt> attributes provide a semantic way to add borders and rounded corners.</p>
    </section>

    <fig>
      <title>Border Specialization</title>
      <image href="src/borders/bordered-section.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>

    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/borders/bordered-section.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/borders/bordered-section.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <section>
      <title>Border Styling</title>
      <p>The <xmlatt>border</xmlatt> attribute also accepts numeric values 1-5 for width. The <xmlatt
        >rounded</xmlatt> attribute 
        supports values 0-5, <codeph>circle</codeph> and <codeph>pill</codeph>.
        The <xmlatt>bordercolor</xmlatt> attribute can be used to set the color of the border.</p>
    </section>

    <fig>
      <title>Border Width</title>
      <image href="src/borders/border-styling.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog margin="t3" style="pills">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/borders/border-styling.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/borders/border-styling.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <fig>
      <title>Border Color</title>
      <image href="src/borders/border-colors.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog margin="t3" style="pills">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/borders/border-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/borders/border-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <fig>
      <title>Rounded Borders</title>
      <image href="src/borders/border-rounding.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog margin="t3" style="pills">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/borders/border-rounding.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/borders/border-rounding.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <fig>
      <title>Border Circle and Pill</title>
      <image href="src/borders/border-circle.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog margin="t3" style="pills">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/borders/border-circle.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/borders/border-circle.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="frames">
      <title>Frame attribute support</title>
      <p>For DITA elements which support the <xmlatt>frame</xmlatt> attribute, such as <xmlelement>lines</xmlelement>
        and <xmlelement>codeblock</xmlelement>, additional frame borders are automatically added as shown:</p>
    </section>
    <fig>
      <title>Frame attribute support</title>
      <image href="src/borders/frame-attribute-support.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <codeblock>&lt;codeblock frame="sides"&gt;...&lt;/codeblock&gt;
&lt;lines frame="topbot" 
  outputclass="bg-secondary-subtle p-3 border rounded"&gt;
  ...
&lt;/lines&gt;
&lt;table frame="all"&gt;...&lt;/table&gt;</codeblock>
  </body>
</topic>
